      "writtenOn": "2020-03-06T13:02:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can the static configuration be a parameter of the message here instead, and be parameters of startIpv4() instead of \"global\" members ?\n\nIt\u0027s awkward to have 2 public setters that can be called at any time, when the values are actually parameters that are used when starting DHCP. The \"global\" members create state that\u0027s parallel to the StateMachine flow, and it\u0027s easy to get it wrong by getting the two out of sync.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 967,
        "startChar": 21,
        "endLine": 967,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "5ecda9b0144b12e55dc9f5b78ede47f169961277",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "58e3b2be_1725fc52",
        "filename": "packages/Tethering/src/com/android/server/connectivity/tethering/Tethering.java",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 200,
      "author": {
        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-06T13:02:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems really error-prone to track. How about just making it an array of type -\u003e request, for all tethering types that are currently requested ? You might then be able to remove mWifiTetherRequested.\n\nI think having just a set of all requests would be easier as you can keep the invariant that only one of each type is requested at any time, which makes it easier to think about. It\u0027s also easier to justify the array, considering that the request needs to be kept when requesting the interface, so that when the interface shows up parameters are known. I\u0027d clarify it in a comment:\n\n/** Currently active tethering requests per tethering type. Only one of each type can be requested at a time. After a tethering type is requested, the map keeps tethering parameters to be used after the interface comes up asynchronously. */",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 200,
        "startChar": 54,
        "endLine": 200,
        "endChar": 81
      },
      "revId": "5ecda9b0144b12e55dc9f5b78ede47f169961277",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a158bc39_e9d3faa6",
        "filename": "packages/Tethering/src/com/android/server/connectivity/tethering/Tethering.java",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 509,
      "author": {
        "id": 1288034
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-06T13:02:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we just say that calls to startTethering when tethering was already requested for the same type will be ignored ?\nI think it would be hard to manage if the tethering configuration has to be updated on the fly when startTethering is called with different parameters, and it\u0027s also confusing as an API.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 507,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 509,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "5ecda9b0144b12e55dc9f5b78ede47f169961277",
